record evidence-intake-project.papercut.capturing-the-winsafe-gui-for-evidence-took/1 : papercut {
    title "Capturing the WinSafe GUI for evidence took three tries: PowerShell is…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Capturing the WinSafe GUI for evidence took three tries: PowerShell is DPI-unaware by default, so GetWindowRect and PrintWindow returned a downscaled, cropped view of a 150%-DPI window and the lower half of the layout appeared to be missing controls that were actually there. SetProcessDpiAwarenessContext(-4) at the top of the capture script fixes it. Also, GetWindowText across a process boundary returns empty for Edit controls, so a screenshot is the only way to read what the detail pane says. Worth a small scripts/screenshot.ps1 so the next GUI session does not rediscover both.
        """
    observed_at git:15f84a997f9c9c108341d58335ed1f04853861f2
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-30
}

