record evidence-intake-project.papercut.i-passed-scope-terms-as-path-src-gui-winsafe-rs/1 : papercut {
    title "I passed scope terms as \"path src/gui/winsafe.rs\" to knowledge.propose,…"
    state verified
    statement """
        I passed scope terms as "path src/gui/winsafe.rs" to knowledge.propose, copying the `path "..."` form the generated views render, and it was accepted silently — producing scope `path "path src/gui/winsafe.rs"`, a glob that can never match a file, so the records would never have gone stale when winsafe.rs changed. Nothing validates that a scope glob is well-formed or warns that it currently matches zero paths. A warning when a path term matches nothing in the worktree would have caught this at propose time instead of three records later.
        """
    observed_at git:f807e4656fc87aeaa071e01145cf3ebae831b03c
    about "akr"
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-10
}

record evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-explain-crashed-with-akr-x099/1 : papercut {
    title "knowledge.explain crashed with AKR-X099 (internal) for both `decision`…"
    state verified
    statement """
        knowledge.explain crashed with AKR-X099 (internal) for both `decision` and `constraint` after knowledge.propose rejected my slots with AKR-T002. The propose error names the bad slot but not the valid ones, and explain -- the documented way to find them -- is exactly what fails, so I had to read .akr/records/*.akr by hand to learn that a decision uses `decision` plus `claim` blocks and has no `rationale` or `note` slot. Suggest AKR-T002 list the kind's valid slots inline.
        """
    observed_at git:a346f4cfdef94e0f0874cb937583c0e064468c0b
    about "akr"
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-10
}

record evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-propose-returns-lock-stale-true-on/1 : papercut {
    title "knowledge.propose returns lock_stale:true on every write but does not…"
    state verified
    statement """
        knowledge.propose returns lock_stale:true on every write but does not refresh akr.lock, so a later knowledge.validate fails with AKR-R052 ("akr.lock has no hash for <the record I just wrote>"). The fix is `akr lock --update`, but nothing in the propose result or the diagnostic says so, and AGENTS.md's "never hand-edit .akr/" made me hesitant to touch the lock at all. Suggest either refreshing the lock as part of propose, or having AKR-R052 name `akr lock --update` as the remedy.
        """
    observed_at git:a346f4cfdef94e0f0874cb937583c0e064468c0b
    about "akr"
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-10
}

record evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-revise-on-a-proposed-decision-in/1 : papercut {
    title "knowledge.revise on a proposed decision (in-place, rev stays 1)…"
    state verified
    statement """
        knowledge.revise on a proposed decision (in-place, rev stays 1) silently dropped the record's source attributions when `sources` was omitted, and passing `sources` explicitly on a later revise did not write them back (content hash unchanged, no `source` block in the file); knowledge.propose with the same payload had persisted them. Also, propose rejects a source with start_line/end_line alone (needs start_byte/end_byte too) which forces callers to compute byte offsets by hand.
        """
    observed_at git:ca09910b8adc43f55720ac1a9ba05a9064de0734
    about "akr"
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-19
}

